---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { SITE } from '../consts';

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// TEMPLATE. Two things must be decided by you before this is accurate:
//
//   1. GOVERNING_LAW below. You operate from the Philippines and your audience
//      is in the United States. Which law governs is a real choice with real
//      consequences, and it is not one to guess at. Pick deliberately.
//   2. Whether you are trading as an individual or a registered business. If
//      you register an entity later, the operator name here must change.
//
// This is a solid starting template, not legal advice.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

const GOVERNING_LAW = 'the Republic of the Philippines';
const OPERATOR = 'Rona Jane Sabatin';
const CONTACT_EMAIL = 'hello@thegoodhomelist.online';
const updated = new Date().toLocaleDateString('en-US', {
  year: 'numeric', month: 'long', day: 'numeric',
});
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Terms and Conditions"
  description={`The terms governing use of ${SITE.name}, including content accuracy, affiliate links, external sites and limitation of liability.`}
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Terms and Conditions' }]} />
    <article class="read prose">
      <h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
      <p class="muted">Last updated: {updated}</p>

      <p>
        These terms govern your use of {SITE.name} at
        {' '}<a href={SITE.url}>{SITE.url.replace('https://', '')}</a>. By using the site you
        agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use the site.
      </p>
      <p>
        The site is operated by {OPERATOR}. You can reach us at
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>What this site is</h2>
      <p>
        {SITE.name} publishes buying guides, product comparisons and how-to articles about home
        products. It is an independent publication. It does not sell products, process payments,
        hold inventory, or ship anything.
      </p>
      <p>
        Every purchase you make happens on a third-party retailer's site, under that retailer's
        terms. We are not a party to that transaction.
      </p>

      <h2>Content is information, not professional advice</h2>
      <p>
        Our articles are general information based on research and, where stated, hands-on use.
        They are not professional advice.
      </p>
      <p>
        Some guides touch on electrical work, plumbing, tools, structural fixings and home
        maintenance. Those tasks carry real risk of injury and property damage, and the right
        answer depends on your specific home, local building codes and your own competence. Where
        a job involves electricity, gas, water supply, structural elements or working at height,
        engage a qualified professional. Follow the manufacturer's instructions for any product
        over anything written here.
      </p>
      <p>
        You are responsible for deciding whether any suggestion is appropriate for your situation.
      </p>

      <h2>Accuracy and product information</h2>
      <p>
        We work to keep guides accurate and update them as products change, but we cannot
        guarantee that everything is correct or current at the moment you read it. Products get
        revised, discontinued and reformulated without notice.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not publish prices on this site, precisely because they change too often to state
        reliably. Always check the current price, specification, availability and description on
        the retailer's own page before buying. The retailer's listing is authoritative, not ours.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you find an error, tell us at
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> and we will correct the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Affiliate links</h2>
      <p>
        This site contains affiliate links, including links to Amazon.com. If you buy through one,
        we may earn a commission at no additional cost to you. As an Amazon Associate, I earn from
        qualifying purchases.
      </p>
      <p>
        Commission rates do not influence our rankings or recommendations. Our full position is
        set out in the <a href="/affiliate-disclosure/">affiliate disclosure</a> and the
        {' '}<a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>External sites</h2>
      <p>
        We link to third-party websites. We do not control them and are not responsible for their
        content, their products, their privacy practices or your dealings with them. A link is not
        an endorsement of everything on the destination site.
      </p>

      <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        The written content, layout and original images on this site belong to {OPERATOR} unless
        stated otherwise. You are welcome to quote a short extract with a visible link back to the
        source page. You may not republish articles in whole or substantial part, or use our
        content to train a commercial model, without written permission.
      </p>
      <p>
        Product names, brand names and logos mentioned on this site belong to their respective
        owners. Their use here is for identification and commentary. It does not imply any
        affiliation with or endorsement by those owners. Amazon and the Amazon logo are trademarks
        of Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you believe content here infringes your copyright, email
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a> with details of the work and
        the page in question, and we will review it promptly.
      </p>

      <h2>Acceptable use</h2>
      <p>You agree not to:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Use the site for any unlawful purpose</li>
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the site or its infrastructure</li>
        <li>Scrape or copy the site systematically for republication</li>
        <li>Introduce malicious code or attempt to disrupt the service</li>
        <li>Misrepresent your identity when contacting us</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We aim to keep the site available but do not guarantee uninterrupted access. We may
        change, suspend or discontinue any part of it at any time without notice.
      </p>

      <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        The site and its content are provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis, without
        warranties of any kind, express or implied, to the fullest extent permitted by law.
      </p>
      <p>
        To the fullest extent permitted by law, we are not liable for any indirect, incidental or
        consequential loss arising from your use of this site, from reliance on its content, or
        from any product you purchase through a link on it. This does not limit any liability
        that cannot lawfully be excluded, including liability for death or personal injury caused
        by negligence, or for fraud.
      </p>
      <p>
        Any dispute you have about a product belongs with the retailer or manufacturer who sold it
        to you.
      </p>

      <h2>Privacy</h2>
      <p>
        How we handle information is covered in our <a href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a>
        {' '}and <a href="/cookie-policy/">cookie policy</a>, which form part of these terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms. The current version is always the one on this page, with the
        date shown at the top. Continuing to use the site after a change means you accept the
        updated terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Governing law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the laws of {GOVERNING_LAW}, without regard to conflict of law
        rules. Nothing here removes any consumer protection right you have under the mandatory law
        of the country you live in.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms go to
        {' '}<a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
